WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.240
This war...

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:12.820
We're not winning it.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.540
If you speak a word of what I'm about to show you, you will be executed for high treason.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:18.920
It's beautiful.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.240
It's the greatest encryption device in history and the Germans use it for all communications.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.460
Everyone thinks Enigma is unbreakable.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.700
Let me try and we'll know for sure.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.980
Mr. Turing, do you know how many died because of it?

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:33.780
I don't.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:34.460
Three.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.660
While we've been having this conversation.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:39.820
Gentlemen...

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.540
Meet Mr. Turing.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:41.880
We are to work together, then?

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.580
I'm afraid these men would only slow me down.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.060
Popular at school, were you?

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.040
We're short on staff.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.480
We get more staff, then.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.280
You have six minutes to complete the task.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.420
Is that even possible?

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:54.060
No.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:54.700
Takes me eight.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.920
Five minutes and thirty-four seconds.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.220
You said to do it in under six.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.800
What is it that we're really doing?

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.080
We're going to break an unbreakable Nazi code and win the war.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.000
Oh...

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.400
You know, to pull off this irascible genius routine, one actually has to be a genius.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.680
I'm designing a machine that will allow us to break every message every day.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:18.720
Instantly.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.620
You're going to need all the help you can get.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.580
And they are not going to help you if they do not like you.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.080
Have you decrypted a single German message?

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.720
You will never understand the importance of what I am creating here!

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.200
Our patience has expired.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.040
No!

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.420
If you fire Alan...

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:38.720
Well, then, you'll have to fire me.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:39.860
Me, too.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.580
And me.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.420
It had better bloody work.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.840
Alan, you do not have to do this alone.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.260
What are you doing?

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:49.940
What's going on?

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.200
The Navy thinks that one of us is a Soviet spy.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.440
You've got more secrets than the best of them.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.160
What if I don't fancy her in that way?

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.580
You can't tell anyone, Alan.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.300
It's illegal.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:05.640
I'm just a mathematician.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.060
Sometimes, it is the people who no one imagines anything of.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.420
Who do the things that no one...

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:13.900
Can imagine.

